'''Alessandro "Ale" Massagué''' (born 25 March 1987) is a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] politician, currently serving as the incumbent [[Secretariat of Climate and the Environment (Balisca)|Secretary of Climate and the Environment]], since December 2018, and as a confederal delegate representing [[Sanaüja (commune district)|Sanaüja]]. Massagué attended the [[University of Poblenou]], ultimately earning a degree in [[W:Ecological economics|ecological economics]]. Massagué's ideology has been described by political scientists as heavily influenced by [[W:Green anarchism|ecological anarchism]], with an emphasis on [[W:Degrowth|degrowth]], [[W:environmental justice|environmental justice]], [[W:Alter-globalization|alter-globalization]], and [[W:Global justice movement|global justice]]. 

Massagué was a candidate for the [[2021 Baliscan premiership election|premiership in 2021]] following the his re-election in the [[2021 Baliscan confederal election|2021 confederal elections]]. Despite initially low expectations, his campaign generated significant grassroots enthusiasm tied with significant inroads into urban areas by [[Ecological Action|Ecologists]]. Massagué's strong showing in the early debates made him a front-runner in a historically large field of candidates for the premiership. He was ultimately defeated by [[Zavier Bilal]], who received 61.1% of the vote. Bilal later nominated Massagué to be the Secretary for of Climate and the Environment.

Massagué is openly-gay, and is one of eight [[W:LGBTQ|LGBTQ]] members of the [[Bilal II Council|current]] confederal administration of Balisca and 143 incumbent LGBTQ-identifying confederal delegates.

